  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ai-access",
      "text": "AI graph access\nResource-oriented graph tools + bounded context; @mentions identify resources without attaching raw JSON/media.",
      "tags": [
        "ai",
        "backend"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 720,
          "y": 80
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block-a-live-draft-core",
      "text": "Block A: Live draft core\nCurrent: implemented and verified. Core has a location-scoped in-memory ArchitectureDraft service keyed by resource ID, base revision/digest tracking, live load/patch/query/context/list overlay methods, explicit draft get/patch/commit/discard/reload operations, and stale saved-base conflicts.\nVerified by focused core tests and package typecheck.",
      "tags": [
        "backend",
        "core",
        "implementation-block",
        "implemented",
        "sync",
        "verified",
        "workstream-a"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 854,
          "y": 1402
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block-b-editor-binding",
      "text": "Block B: Editor draft binding\nCurrent: implemented and verified. React Flow editor/panel now binds to live draft APIs/events. Local editor edits patch the live draft, remote/AI draft events update the editor state, and the editor remains journal/undo aware.\nSave commits the live draft; Reload discards/reloads saved state instead of acting as an editing path.\nVerified by app architecture tests, app typecheck, and app production build.",
      "tags": [
        "frontend",
        "implementation-block",
        "implemented",
        "sync",
        "verified",
        "workstream-b"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1254,
          "y": 1402
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block-c-live-first-tools",
      "text": "Block C: Live-first graph tools\nCurrent: implemented and verified. Core ArchitectureTools, legacy opencode GraphTools, and Code Mode native graph tools use live-draft edits by default with saved fallback and source metadata.\nReload now means saved reload/discard. Live inspection uses list/query/context/live-aware paths instead.\nVerified by core tools tests, opencode graph/code-mode tests, typechecks, and HTTP draft route coverage.",
      "tags": [
        "ai",
        "backend",
        "implementation-block",
        "implemented",
        "tools",
        "verified",
        "workstream-c"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1654,
          "y": 1402
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block-d-save-reload-boundary",
      "text": "Block D: Save/reload boundary\nCurrent: implemented and verified for normal edit-live/save/reload semantics. Draft patch edits stay in memory; explicit commit/save writes to managed resource; discard/reload drops the live draft and returns saved state.\nPublic draft routes and generated clients exist for get, patch, commit, discard, and reload.\nVerified by schema/core/client/app/opencode tests, route exerciser coverage for draft routes, and app build.",
      "tags": [
        "backend",
        "frontend",
        "implementation-block",
        "implemented",
        "storage",
        "verified",
        "workstream-d"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2054,
          "y": 1402
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block-e-conflict-lifecycle",
      "text": "Block E: Conflict + lifecycle rules\nCurrent: partial implemented. Stale saved-base conflicts, draft discard/reload, remove/reset cleanup, and draft update/discard events are implemented.\nRemaining follow-up: deeper multi-window ownership/transfer policy, closed-window ownership cleanup UX, and exhaustive external disk-change user flows.\nCurrent normal edit-live/save/reload shift does not require loading/reloading as an editing path anymore.",
      "tags": [
        "backend",
        "follow-up",
        "frontend",
        "implementation-block",
        "partial-implemented",
        "remaining",
        "storage",
        "workstream-e"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1054,
          "y": 1672
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block-f-focused-tests",
      "text": "Block F: Focused tests + hardening\nCurrent: implemented for this shift, with follow-up coverage still possible for advanced ownership. Added/updated tests for draft patch persistence boundary, commit/discard/reload, stale saved-base conflict, live-first tools, editor draft events/helpers, generated client surface, legacy/Code Mode parity, and HTTP draft route scenarios.\nVerified package typechecks pass across schema/core/protocol/server/client/app/opencode; focused tests and app build pass.",
      "tags": [
        "implementation",
        "implementation-block",
        "implemented",
        "test",
        "verified",
        "workstream-f"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1854,
          "y": 1672
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "current-graph-tools",
      "text": "Current Graph tools\nResource: list/create/rename/delete/reload/context/query.\nNodes/tags: create/update/delete nodes, set tag colors.\nWires/layout: connect/update/disconnect wires, batch layout.\nBulk: batch edit for many nodes/wires/tags at once.",
      "tags": [
        "ai",
        "backend",
        "tools"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 427.93749403980075,
          "y": 713.9947929056739
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "editor-subscribe-patches",
      "text": "Editor subscribes to patches\nCurrent: implemented. App event handling recognizes draft updated/discarded events and updates the draft query/cache so live draft changes can flow into React Flow editor state.\nLocal editor edits patch the live draft and remain part of the same journal/save/reload workflow.",
      "tags": [
        "frontend",
        "implementation",
        "implemented",
        "sync",
        "verified"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2006.658728403409,
          "y": 865.5802197681782
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "guardrails",
      "text": "Product guardrails\nKeep graphs authored and conversational. No deterministic analyzers, fixed taxonomy, or generated source-of-truth model.",
      "tags": [
        "core"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 720,
          "y": 300
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lifecycle-conflict-rules",
      "text": "Define lifecycle + conflict rules\nCurrent: partial implemented. Stale saved-base conflict, draft discard/reload, commit boundary, and remove/reset cleanup are implemented.\nRemaining follow-up: formal multi-window ownership/transfer and closed-window cleanup policy beyond the basic live draft lifecycle.",
      "tags": [
        "backend",
        "follow-up",
        "frontend",
        "implementation",
        "partial-implemented",
        "remaining"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1582.9670990675259,
          "y": 1085.5331124107302
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "live-document-service",
      "text": "Implement live document service\nCurrent: implemented. ArchitectureDraft plus ArchitectureGraph live/draft methods provide the shared in-memory resource draft keyed by resource ID, with base revision/digest and explicit commit/discard/reload operations.\nEditor, AI tools, legacy tools, and Code Mode now route through the live draft path where appropriate.",
      "tags": [
        "core",
        "implementation",
        "implemented",
        "sync",
        "verified"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1274.721599304349,
          "y": 825.8130299050473
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "live-draft-gap",
      "text": "Live draft gap\nCurrent: closed for the normal software shift. AI tools and the React editor now operate through live draft APIs, edits stay live until Save/commit, and Reload/discard means saved-state reload rather than editing.\nRemaining follow-up is narrower: advanced multi-window ownership/lifecycle hardening.",
      "tags": [
        "ai",
        "frontend",
        "implemented",
        "target",
        "verified"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1488.0069647972407,
          "y": 521.0588667119911
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "live-draft-tests",
      "text": "Add focused tests\nCurrent: implemented for the normal live edit/save/reload shift. Coverage includes core draft behavior, tool routing/source metadata, app draft event/helpers, client generated surface, legacy/Code Mode parity, HTTP draft routes, package typechecks, and app build.\nFollow-up: deeper multi-window ownership/transfer tests if that policy is expanded.",
      "tags": [
        "follow-up",
        "implementation",
        "implemented",
        "test",
        "verified"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 1961.2364394119245,
          "y": 1084.172849854106
        }
      }
    },
